prompt:
A developer runs the following against an empty table t on a database that supports savepoints:

BEGIN;
INSERT INTO t VALUES ('A');
SAVEPOINT s1;
INSERT INTO t VALUES ('B');
ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT s1;
INSERT INTO t VALUES ('C');
COMMIT;

Which rows does t contain afterwards?

A support engineer intends to deactivate one account and runs:

UPDATE accounts SET status = 'inactive';

in a session with autocommit enabled. What is the result?

A product-list page only displays product names and prices. Reviewing the ORM-generated SQL shows:

SELECT id, name, price, description, spec_sheet_pdf, image_blob FROM products;

The page is slow and network traffic from the database is high. What is the best remediation?

An ORM generates the following query for a login lookup on a table with an ordinary index on email:

SELECT * FROM users WHERE LOWER(email) = LOWER(?);

The execution plan shows a full table scan. Why, and how can it be remediated?

An ORM-generated paging query becomes slower the further users page through results:

SELECT * FROM events ORDER BY event_id LIMIT 50 OFFSET 200000;

What explains the slowdown, and which remediation is common?

During a code audit, a reviewer finds this inside a stored procedure:

SET @sql = 'SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer = ''' + @customerName + '''';
EXEC(@sql);

What is the main issue?
